  "title": "Kirby Problem 5.13",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $M$ be a finite-volume hyperbolic $n$-manifold.\n\n- Does it always have a finite cover with $b_{1}>0$?\n\n- Does it always have a finite cover with fundamental group that surjects onto a non-abelian free group?\n\n- Does it have a finite cover with cubulated fundamental group?\n\n- When $n$ is odd, does it always have a finite cover that fibers over the circle?",
